  id: buffalo
  displayName: Buffalo
  habitat: Woodland and grassland near water. See them at Lake Nakuru National Park.
  status: Near Threatened (IUCN Red List)
  fact: 'Buffalo herds are largely matriarchal: the core of a herd is adult females
    and their young. In open country, a large herd offers protection from lions.'
  viewingTip: Give a lone bull a very wide berth. Buffalo are unpredictable and are
    treated as one of the most dangerous animals in Africa, so never walk towards
    one.
  warningLine: The buffalo is pawing the ground. Back off.
  viewingRadius: 15
  dangerRadius: 6
